                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I love point and click adventures, so I was really looking forward to this one since it has such positive reviews.\n\nThis was quite possibly the worst point and click game I've ever played.\n\nIt wasn't all bad; the hand-drawn animations were good and although it was extremely short (~2.5 hours even with me getting stuck at one point because a puzzle wasn't working properly) the story was decent and there were some good puzzles. There were also some bad puzzles, though, and several annoying quicktime events that got repetitive quickly.\n\nFor me, the nail in the coffin was the lack of dialogue. The main character glares angrily for the entire game and never speaks, and with one exception none of the others do either. Point and click adventures thrive on the humor from talking to different characters and the main character commenting on things. There was none of that.\n\nEven getting it on sale, I regret buying this.",
